# talus_patch: a heap of broken rock fanning out below a gully (BUILD_PLAN
# S5 brief B5): solid stones in the boulders' language, each a slate (2)
# body with its top glacier blue (3) on the lit side, of uneven sizes,
# a big one at the back and smaller ones before it, overlapping its foot,
# each stone's lit top open to the sky above it (never ringed by another
# stone's shade, so none reads as a hole); no hollow outline and no dark
# dash inside it (nothing to read as a net, a slit or an eye); its ground
# line ink (0). The anchor, 0,0, is the middle of its ground line. 24
# wide, 10 tall.
C 2  L -3,-8  L -4,-7 -3,-7  L -5,-6 -2,-6  L -6,-5 -1,-5
     L 2,-5  L -11,-4  L -6,-4 3,-4  L -12,-3 -10,-3
     L -6,-3 5,-3  L 8,-3  L -12,-2 -8,-2  L -6,-2 10,-2
     L -12,-1 11,-1
C 3  L -2,-9 -1,-9  L -2,-8 0,-8  L -2,-7 0,-7  L -1,-6 0,-6
     L 3,-6 4,-6  L -10,-5 -9,-5  L 0,-5  L 3,-5 5,-5
     L -10,-4 -8,-4  L 4,-4 6,-4  L 9,-4 10,-4  L -9,-3 -8,-3
     L 6,-3 7,-3  L 9,-3 11,-3  L -7,-2  L 11,-2
C 0  L -12,0 11,0
